==Enemy==
Arguably the strongest variant of [[Otta-smack-u]], this enemy is more often than not a monstrosity to behold. Its base stats are already pretty high for a peon, and this is further exacerbated by late-game buffs, not to mention its low money drop. It moves faster and has two additional knockbacks to negate its heavy pushing power, though its 50% chance to cause knockback can easily turn the tables alongside its piercing Omni Strikes that hit up to 200 range away. If that wasn't enough, its [[Counter-Surge]] ability can potentially bring forth destruction from a great distance when it comes into play.

==Strategy==
Like [[St. Dober]] and [[Angelic Gory]], this enemy is not really dangerous by itself since it's vulnerable to status effects like Slow, meaning crowd-controllers like [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]] might be able to stall it just fine, even with its Omni Strike. It becomes threatening when backed by other threats, however, as its knockback ability allows enemies to advance very easily and it can reposition two times. Alongside accounting for its support, you should consider units that can outrange and deal heavy damage to this enemy to remove it from play before things turn awry. An extremely potent counter to Gokurakko is [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], being able to disable its Knockback by Cursing it and dealing an immense amount of DPS.

If you're concerned about it spawning Surges, simply don't use [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]] so it doesn't get the chance, or bring [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune units]].

